Terrain r22 adapts all twelve Populators/VolcanoPopulator recipes, nested domain
warps, Ridge/Billow, Cubic, Worley, Steps and terrace constructions. It uses
upstream Perlin gradient hashing and CURVE3 interpolation, seeded graph selection,
block-based amplitude settings and continuous terrace transitions. Dormant volcanoes
have no lava pipe. Erosion displacements and sediment volumes are converted to
block units on the persisted grid; full-height smoothing uses the upstream
1.8-block kernel. This is not a bit-for-bit reproduction of upstream worlds.

